PRS-CS (github.com/getian107/PRScs, MIT, LICENSE here) files as patched for the bench-sim all-variant arm; they replace
the same files of the install that prscs_auto.PRSCS points at. PRS-CS's own model, priors, iterations, burn-in,
thinning and draw order are unchanged; with no environment variable set its code runs as released, apart from the set
membership in parse_ldblk (output bit-identical).

- parse_genet.py: set membership in parse_ldblk; parse_ldblk split into the hdf5 read and prepare_ldblk (selection, sign
  flips, symmetrization), callable on blocks in memory (prscs_auto_allvar.py runs PRS-CS's functions in-process
  that way instead of through an hdf5 file); PRSCS_LD_CACHE saves/loads parse_ldblk's output. PRSCS_DEVICE=gpu:
  the selection and flips are skipped when they are the identity (bit-identical), and the symmetrization is computed
  on the GPU by the symmetric eigendecomposition, Q|L|Q' = the SVD's V' diag(s) V (9e-14 relative to scipy's SVD on a
  6,922 block); the prepared blocks stay on the device when they fit.
- mcmc_gtb.py: PRSCS_DEVICE=gpu runs each block's Cholesky, triangular solves and quadratic form in float64 on CuPy,
  every draw still on the host in PRS-CS's order; with several visible GPUs the blocks are shared out by Cholesky cost
  and updated concurrently (independent given psi and sigma), quadratic forms summed in block order. The sums over
  variants use numpy's in place of Python's builtin sum. PRSCS_GIG=vector draws psi for all variants at once.
  mcmc returns the posterior means (for validation).
- gigrnd.py: gigrnd_vec, the same Devroye sampler over arrays.

Validations: validate_gpu.py (one real 6,922-variant block: GPU chain equals CPU chain to 8e-15 over 5 iterations;
eigh symmetrization 9e-14); validate_multi.sh/.py (CPU, 1-GPU and 2-GPU samplers on 5 synthetic blocks, 5 iterations:
2e-15); validate_gig.py (KS of gigrnd_vec against gigrnd and scipy's GIG, 8 parameter sets, 1e5 draws, all P > 0.1).
bench_step.py times the block step's operations (H100: dpotrf ~22 TF fp64, 233 ms at 25k). run_gpu.sh is the MSI
launcher (16-stream prefetch of the cohort genotypes into page cache, the harness under the GPU venv).
